b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6), conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation and of the application of a relation not yet defined until it can be decided, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 6: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the known sequence s of b = s ++ c. Elements are integers. No other stage has constants;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P08a, and P08b, which is its stages 1 to 3. Unknown sequences a, b, c, and unknown elements x, y, z. Stage 1: a = the sequence of x, y, z. Stage 2: rev(a, b), with rev not yet defined. Stage 3: x = y. Stage 4: the definitions of rev and conc, as in P03, which arrive together. Stage 5: y = z. Stage 6: b = s ++ c. ALGOL 60 has no definitions that arrive while a program runs: the procedures rev and conc are in the text, and the Boolean defined says whether their definition has arrived. An application of rev before then is held as posed, awaiting the definition, and is neither true nor false: the fourth of the problem's four states, the open reading. When the definition has arrived it is decided as rev and conc compute it. An element of a sequence is an index into the arrays ek and ev, a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it: 1 is x, 2 is y, 3 is z, and the elements of s are further indices, each with its value. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence of the element hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c]. rev and conc move elements and never look at their values, so they work on elements that have none. Each unknown sequence is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it. Each relation is held as posed until enough of its places are known, when it gives the remaining place its value or is tested. Every held relation is examined in the order posed, again and again, until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, j, top, nel, av, bv, cv, sv, held, pass, rev1, rev2, conc1, conc2;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ak, bk, ck, q1, q2, q3, q5, q6, defined, changed, inconsistent;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl, ev[1:1000];
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ ek[1:1000];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence of the element h followed by the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ sameel(e, f);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e, f; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e, f;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the equality of two elements: the same unknown, or two values that are equal. Two different unknowns are not taken as equal: no test here meets one;
  sameel := i̲f̲ e = f t̲h̲e̲n̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ek[e] ∧ ek[f] t̲h̲e̲n̲ ev[e] = ev[f] e̲l̲s̲e̲ f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ same(p, q);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p, q; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p, q;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the equality of two sequences, element by element;
  same := i̲f̲ p = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q = 0 e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ q = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ sameel(hd[p], hd[q]) t̲h̲e̲n̲ same(tl[p], tl[q]) e̲l̲s̲e̲ f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ conc(a, b);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, b; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ conc(a, b, c), computing c from a and b by its cases, in order. Case 1: conc(the empty sequence, b, b). Case 2: conc(h followed by a, b, h followed by c) if conc(a, b, c);
  i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ conc1 := conc1 + 1; conc := b e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c;
    conc2 := conc2 + 1;
    c := conc(tl[a], b);
    conc := cons(hd[a], c)
  e̲n̲d̲ conc;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ rev(a);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ rev(a, b), computing b from a by its cases, in order. Case 1: rev(the empty sequence, the empty sequence). Case 2: rev(h followed by l, r) if rev(l, q) and conc(q, the sequence of h alone, r);
  i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ rev1 := rev1 + 1; rev := 0 e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ q;
    rev2 := rev2 + 1;
    q := rev(tl[a]);
    rev := conc(q, cons(hd[a], 0))
  e̲n̲d̲ rev;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ equal(e, f);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e, f; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e, f;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of an equation between two elements, held until one of them is known: it gives the other its value, or tests it when both are known. It is decided at once, in the evaluator of b = s ++ c, where one of them is always known;
  i̲f̲ ek[e] ∧ ek[f] t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ev[e] ≠ ev[f] t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ek[e] t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ ev[f] := ev[e]; ek[f] := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ek[f] t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ ev[e] := ev[f]; ek[e] := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine1;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of a = the sequence of x, y, z: with a unknown, a is given that value. With a known it would be tested, which no stage reaches;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ ak t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬same(av, cons(1, cons(2, cons(3, 0)))) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ av := cons(1, cons(2, cons(3, 0))); ak := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    q1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine1;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of the application rev(a, b): held while the definition of rev and conc has not arrived, and while a is unknown. Then b is computed from a by rev, or tested if known;
  i̲f̲ defined ∧ ak t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ r;
    r := rev(av);
    i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬same(bv, r) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ bv := r; bk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    q2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine2;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine3;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of x = y, held until one of them is known;
  i̲f̲ ek[1] ∨ ek[2] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ equal(1, 2); q3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲ examine3;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine5;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of y = z, held until one of them is known;
  i̲f̲ ek[2] ∨ ek[3] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ equal(2, 3); q5 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲ examine5;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine6;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of b = s ++ c. With b known, each element of s is equated with the element of b in its place, which gives that element its value or tests it, and c is the rest of b, or is tested with it. With b unknown and c known, b is s ++ c. With both unknown, it waits;
  i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p, e, w;
    p := bv; e := sv;
    f̲o̲r̲ w := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ e ≠ 0 ∧ ¬inconsistent d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ p = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ equal(hd[p], hd[e]); p := tl[p]; e := tl[e] e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ ck t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬same(cv, p) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ cv := p; ck := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    q6 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ck t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ w, e, first, last, c;
    first := last := 0; e := sv;
    f̲o̲r̲ w := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ e ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c := cons(hd[e], 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := c e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := c;
      last := c; e := tl[e]
    e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ bv := cv e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ tl[last] := cv; bv := first e̲n̲d̲;
    bk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲; q6 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine6;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every held relation is examined, in the order posed, again and again until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ pass := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ changed d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      changed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
      i̲f̲ q1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine1;
      i̲f̲ q2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine2;
      i̲f̲ q3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine3;
      i̲f̲ q5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine5;
      i̲f̲ q6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine6
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ digits(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a natural number, its decimal digits with no sign and no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ digits(v ÷ 10);
    d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
    i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
  e̲n̲d̲ digits;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printint(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, its sign if negative and its digits, with no padding, so that an answer with many values stays on one line;
  i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); digits(-v) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ digits(v);

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printel(e);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an element, its value if known, else the name of its unknown;
  i̲f̲ ek[e] t̲h̲e̲n̲ printint(ev[e]) e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ e = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ e = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`y') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`z');

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ w;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    f̲o̲r̲ w := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ printel(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ seqplace(known, v, name);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, name; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, name;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence in a relation, its value if known, else the name of its unknown, 1 for a, 2 for b, 3 for c;
  i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ printseq(v) e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ name = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`a') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ name = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`b') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`c');

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ seqstate(known, v, inheld, name);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, inheld, name; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known, inheld; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, name;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an unknown sequence, as its value, or held by a relation, or free;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ name = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`a') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ name = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`b') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`c');
    i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); printseq(v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ inheld t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free')
  e̲n̲d̲ seqstate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ elstate(e, inheld);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e, inheld; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ inheld;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an unknown element, as its value, or held by a relation, or free;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ e = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ e = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`y') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`z');
    i̲f̲ ek[e] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); printint(ev[e]) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ inheld t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free')
  e̲n̲d̲ elstate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the relations held, in the order posed, separated by commas, with the values known put in their places;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ first;
    first := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    i̲f̲ q1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ seqplace(ak, av, 1); PRINTTEXT(` = (x, y, z)'); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      PRINTTEXT(`rev('); seqplace(ak, av, 1); PRINTTEXT(`, '); seqplace(bk, bv, 2); PRINTTEXT(`)');
      i̲f̲ ¬defined t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` awaiting its definition');
      first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q3 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, '); printel(1); PRINTTEXT(` = '); printel(2); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q5 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, '); printel(2); PRINTTEXT(` = '); printel(3); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q6 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      seqplace(bk, bv, 2); PRINTTEXT(` = '); printseq(sv); PRINTTEXT(` ++ '); seqplace(ck, cv, 3)
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  ak := bk := ck := q1 := q2 := q3 := q5 := q6 := defined := inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  top := rev1 := rev2 := conc1 := conc2 := 0;
  f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ 3 d̲o̲ ek[j] := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  nel := 3; sv := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q1 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q3 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ defined := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ q5 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the sequence s: each element, in order, is a new element with its value;
      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len, e, first, last, c;
      len := read;
      first := last := 0;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        e := read; nel := nel + 1; ev[nel] := e; ek[nel] := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
        c := cons(nel, 0);
        i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := c e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := c;
        last := c
      e̲n̲d̲;
      sv := first; q6 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    propagate;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown, and the relations still held;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
      seqstate(ak, av, q1 ∨ q2, 1); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      seqstate(bk, bv, q2 ∨ q6, 2); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      seqstate(ck, cv, q6, 3); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      elstate(1, q3); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      elstate(2, q3 ∨ q5); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      elstate(3, q5);
      i̲f̲ q1 ∨ q2 ∨ q3 ∨ q5 ∨ q6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the relations held, the application awaiting its definition, the values known, and the applications of each case of rev and conc;
    held := (i̲f̲ q1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ q3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ q5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ q6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0);
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`held relations: ');
    i̲f̲ held = 0 ∧ ¬q2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ defined t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`rev and conc: defined'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`rev and conc: not yet defined'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q2 ∧ ¬defined t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`rev(a, b): held as posed, awaiting the definition of rev, neither true nor false'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ak t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind a]'); printseq(av); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind b]'); printseq(bv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ck t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind c]'); printseq(cv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ek[1] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); print(ev[1]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ek[2] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind y]'); print(ev[2]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ ek[3] t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind z]'); print(ev[3]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ q2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended pending-applications 1]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ held > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); print(held); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations rev/1 '); print(rev1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations rev/2 '); print(rev2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/1 '); print(conc1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/2 '); print(conc2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
